Something that niggles me about our beloved game is undead turning.
There is a big difference between a live kitten and an undead kitten
but if in nethack I zap my /oUT at a kitten corpse, I get the former
and not the latter.

Therefore I suggest the reanimation properties of undead turning be
changed to something more in keeping with its name, so that corpses
re-animated with UT come back undead rather than alive. Most of UT's
other functions would remain unchanged. This might force change in the
way the game handles zombies (it would have to allow all kinds of
arbitrary foo zombies) but I don't see that as a bad thing. I believe
[s] already does this with its necromancers and their 'raise zombies'
technique.

Obviously this also changes game balance, because bringing corpses to
life (rather than to undeath) is a useful part of the game: storing and
refreshing corpses, retrying for dragon scales, reviving pets and so
on. Therefore to fill this gap I would suggest that a new wand be
introduced- the Wand of Life. Aimed wand, no engrave effect, invisible
beam. This would take the /oUT's old effect, ie revification of a
corpse to a living monster (rather than an undead version of it.

This new wand would be quite rare (about as common as a /oDeath, I
guess) and I suppose /oUT should be made a little rarer to fit the new
wand into the item generation balance. It also seems to me a 'wand of
life' would be a comfortable addition to a game that already posesses a
'wand of death'.

Now for the cool bit: Why shouldn't monsters use /oL and /oUT? Zapping
their fallen comrades back into battle would be a powerful weapon for
them and add a startling (but fun) new challenge for players. It would
certainly liven things up for powerful characters, and fits well into
existing game precedents. It would even be in character for (foo) Lichs
to be generated with a / of undead turning from time to time. Muahahah.

